    "original_procedure": "To a solution of 3.862 g of aryl bromide 1 and 3.401 g of boron compound 2 in 80 mL of dioxane and 20 mL of water was added 2.245 g of K2CO3 followed by 0.328 g of (Ph3P)4Pd under N2 with stirring. The mixture was refluxed for several hours until the material was disappeared. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature. The dioxane was removed by rotary evaporation. The residue was poured into water and extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, filtered and the solvent was removed by rotary evaporation. The product was isolated by flash chromatography on silica gel using 10:90 EtOAc-hexanes as eluant. The product was a clear, colorless oil."
