    "original_procedure": "A mixture of methyl trans-3-chlorocinnamate (393.2 mg, 2 mmol), dichlorobis(tricyclohexylphosphine) palladium (73.8 mg, 0.10 mol), phenylboronic acid (292.6 mg, 2.4 mmol), and cesium fluoride (607 mg, 4.0 mmol) in 1-methyl-2-pyrrolidinone (NMP, 5 mL) was degassed by purging with nitrogen. The mixture was then heated at 100 °C for 10 hours. The mixture was then partitioned between ethyl acetate (90 mL) and water (20 mL). The organic layer was separated, washed with water, dried, and concentrated. The residue was then purified by column chromatography eluting with 50/50/5 toluene/hexane/ether to give the coupled product (466 mg, 98%)."
